# Detection, Response & Specific Entities

## 1. Detection & Response Ecosystem (SIEM vs. SOAR)

$$\text{SIEM} = \text{Centralized Detection, Log Protection \& Alerting} \quad \Longleftrightarrow \quad \text{SOAR} = \text{Automated Orchestration \& Instant Response}$$

| Technology | Operational Scope | Key Functionality |
|---|---|---|
| **SIEM** | Centralized Log Collector | Detects threats and generates alerts; **does NOT perform automated actions**. |
| **EDR** | End-user Devices (Endpoints) | Detects, isolates, and remediates endpoint threats (malware, ransomware). |
| **NDR** | Network Traffic & Flows | Analyzes network traffic for anomalies, intrusions, and forensic data. |
| **SOAR** | Workflow Automation | Executes **automated playbooks** (e.g., auto-isolating infected hosts) & enriches threat data. |
| **XDR** | Unified Ecosystem | The integrated suite combining **EDR + NDR + SOAR**. |

