## 3. Entity Type Specific Rules (Section 4.8)

### A. Public Electronic Communications Providers (Sec. 4.8.1)
* In scope regardless of size; classified as **Essential** if medium-sized or larger.
* Must implement **Security by Design/Default**, **End-to-End Encryption**, and **Secure Routing Standards**.
* Subject to jurisdiction in **every Member State** where services are supplied.

### B. Trust Service Providers (TSPs) (Sec. 4.8.2)
* Classified as **Essential Entities** regardless of size.
* **Strict Reporting Rule:** Must report significant incidents within **24 hours** (instead of the standard 72-hour window).

### C. TLD Registries, DNS Services & Cloud/MSPs (Sec. 4.8.3 - 4.8.4)
* **Explicit Exemption:** **Root Name Servers** are completely exempted from NIS2 scope (Article 6(20b)).
* **Jurisdiction:** Governed by the Member State of their **Main Establishment**.
* **Non-EU Entities:** Must designate a legally liable **Representative** within an EU Member State where they operate.
* **TLD SLA Requirement:** TLD registries must respond to lawful information requests within **72 hours**.
